1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,720
World Soccer's governing body, FIFA, selected Canada, Mexico, and the United States to host the 2026 World Cup.

2
00:00:12,519 --> 00:00:23,640
On Wednesday, FIFA Member Countries voted 134-65 for the three nations over the other candidate, Morocco.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,659
The vote marks the first time that FIFA has accepted a three-nation bid for the soccer championship.

4
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:40,920
The public vote took place in Moscow, where the 2018 soccer championship begins on Thursday.

5
00:00:42,439 --> 00:00:46,479
Football is known as soccer in the United States.

6
00:00:47,799 --> 00:00:58,700
The North American bid had to overcome concerns about the effects of policies of the administration of US President Donald Trump.

7
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:07,799
One such policy was a ban on travel from six majority Muslim countries for security reasons.

8
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:21,260
Cameroon's representative to FIFA, Kevin Injomo, said the three-nation bid was strong, and if it was just the United States, Morocco would have beaten them.

9
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:33,019
He added, people have a soft spot for Mexico, especially looking at Mexico as a little bit underdeveloped and giving them a chance.

10
00:01:34,019 --> 00:01:37,180
Canada is a good tourist destination.

11
00:01:39,019 --> 00:01:45,040
The 2026 World Cup will also be the first to include 48 teams.

12
00:01:46,579 --> 00:01:57,579
The US proposed hosting 60 out of the 80 games in 2026. Canada and Mexico would then host 10 games each.

13
00:01:58,579 --> 00:02:05,299
FIFA will have to decide how the games are divided up and which cities will be selected.

14
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:13,159
FIFA will also decide on whether all three countries are guaranteed a place at the tournament.

15
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:21,199
Both the United States and Canada failed to qualify for this year's World Cup.

16
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:29,840
North American officials have promised to deliver $14 billion in revenue from the event.

17
00:02:31,099 --> 00:02:41,500
Preparation for the World Cup will not require major construction work because the 16 stadiums where matches will be played already exist.

18
00:02:42,539 --> 00:02:47,300
Canada will host Men's World Cup matches for the first time.

19
00:02:48,199 --> 00:02:56,120
Mexico last held the event in 1986, while the US held the World Cup in 1994.

20
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,379
I'm Jonathan Evans.

